The locator core of this project (computed ARIA role calculation,
accessible-name computation, anchored light-DOM CSS path building,
the in-page capture/record panel and the recorder event wiring) was
originally developed by the same author for the SAPFX project (a SAP
test-automation ecosystem for Robot Framework, Apache-2.0) and was
ported here, generalized and stripped of all SAP/UI5-specific behaviour.

The HTML documentation-report export (one chapter per scenario, factual
phrase next to the exact keyword line) follows the same concept chain:
it re-implements, per step and without any code reuse, an idea observed
in RoboSAPiens' saveHtmlReport (imbus AG, Apache-2.0), first ported to
the SAPFX web recorder and then brought here. The cross-origin iframe
warning strip is likewise ported from the SAPFX web recorder.
